[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 SDP (Software Development Plan) - ADAS Control Module
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
 Scope
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
1 Identification
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-001
TITLE: Development Plan Identification
STATEMENT: This document shall be identified as the Software Development Plan (SDP) for the Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS) Control Module, version 1.0, following MIL-STD-498 and ISO 26262 development standards.
RATIONALE: Proper development plan identification ensures configuration management and development traceability for safety-critical automotive systems.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
2 System overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-002
TITLE: Development Overview
STATEMENT: The ADAS Control Module development shall follow a safety-critical development process with comprehensive planning, rigorous development practices, and continuous quality assurance for automotive safety applications.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive development overview establishes the foundation for all development activities in the automotive safety domain.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
3 Document overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-003
TITLE: Development Plan Structure
STATEMENT: This document shall be organized into sections covering development process, organization, resources, schedules, and quality assurance following MIL-STD-498 and automotive safety development standards.
RATIONALE: Structured organization facilitates development planning and execution for safety-critical systems.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 2
 Referenced documents
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-004
TITLE: Development References
STATEMENT: The development plan shall reference MIL-STD-498, ISO 26262 development standards, MISRA C++ guidelines, AUTOSAR development standards, and automotive safety development best practices.
RATIONALE: Development references ensure consistency with established automotive safety development patterns.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
 Development process
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
1 Development methodology
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-005
TITLE: Safety-Critical Development Methodology
STATEMENT: The development shall follow a V-model development process with comprehensive requirements analysis, detailed design, rigorous implementation, thorough testing, and continuous validation for safety-critical systems.
RATIONALE: V-model development methodology ensures comprehensive system validation and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-006
TITLE: Iterative Development Process
STATEMENT: The development shall include iterative refinement cycles with continuous integration, automated testing, and regular reviews to ensure quality and safety compliance throughout development.
RATIONALE: Iterative development process ensures continuous quality improvement and early defect detection.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
2 Development phases
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-007
TITLE: Requirements Phase
STATEMENT: The requirements phase shall include comprehensive requirements analysis, safety analysis, risk assessment, and stakeholder validation with complete traceability and documentation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive requirements phase ensures complete system specification and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-008
TITLE: Design Phase
STATEMENT: The design phase shall include architectural design, detailed design, interface design, and safety design with comprehensive review and validation processes.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive design phase ensures system architecture and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-009
TITLE: Implementation Phase
STATEMENT: The implementation phase shall include MISRA C++ compliant coding, code reviews, static analysis, and unit testing with continuous integration and quality assurance.
RATIONALE: Rigorous implementation phase ensures code quality and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-010
TITLE: Testing Phase
STATEMENT: The testing phase shall include comprehensive testing activities including unit testing, integration testing, system testing, safety testing, and field validation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive testing phase ensures system validation and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
 Development organization
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
1 Organizational structure
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-011
TITLE: Development Team Structure
STATEMENT: The development organization shall include dedicated teams for requirements engineering, system design, software development, testing, safety engineering, and quality assurance with clear responsibilities and reporting structures.
RATIONALE: Organized development structure ensures comprehensive coverage and accountability for safety-critical development.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
2 Roles and responsibilities
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-012
TITLE: Project Manager Role
STATEMENT: The project manager shall be responsible for overall project coordination, resource allocation, schedule management, and stakeholder communication for the ADAS development project.
RATIONALE: Clear project management ensures successful project execution and stakeholder satisfaction.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-013
TITLE: Safety Engineer Role
STATEMENT: The safety engineer shall be responsible for safety analysis, risk assessment, safety requirements, and safety validation throughout the development lifecycle.
RATIONALE: Dedicated safety engineering ensures compliance with automotive safety standards.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-014
TITLE: Software Engineer Role
STATEMENT: The software engineer shall be responsible for software design, implementation, testing, and documentation following MISRA C++ and automotive safety guidelines.
RATIONALE: Dedicated software engineering ensures code quality and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
 Development resources
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
1 Personnel requirements
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-015
TITLE: Development Team Requirements
STATEMENT: The development team shall include experienced automotive software engineers, safety engineers, test engineers, and quality assurance specialists with expertise in safety-critical systems.
RATIONALE: Experienced development team ensures successful project execution and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
2 Development tools
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-016
TITLE: Development Environment
STATEMENT: The development environment shall include automotive-grade development tools, MISRA C++ compliant compilers, static analysis tools, and safety analysis tools for comprehensive development support.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive development environment ensures efficient development and quality assurance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-017
TITLE: Testing Tools
STATEMENT: The development shall use automated testing tools, simulation tools, and analysis tools for comprehensive testing and validation support.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive testing tools ensure efficient testing and quality assurance.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 6
 Development schedule
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-018
TITLE: Development Timeline
STATEMENT: The development shall follow a structured timeline with defined milestones, deliverables, and review points throughout the development lifecycle with appropriate buffer time for safety validation.
RATIONALE: Structured development timeline ensures successful project execution and stakeholder satisfaction.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 7
 Quality assurance
[SECTION]
TITLE: 7
1 Quality assurance activities
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-019
TITLE: Code Review Process
STATEMENT: The development shall include mandatory code reviews for all safety-critical code with peer review, automated analysis, and safety review processes.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive code review process ensures code quality and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-020
TITLE: Testing Process
STATEMENT: The development shall include comprehensive testing processes with automated testing, manual testing, safety testing, and continuous integration for quality assurance.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive testing process ensures system quality and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-021
TITLE: Documentation Process
STATEMENT: The development shall include comprehensive documentation processes with requirements documentation, design documentation, test documentation, and user documentation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive documentation process ensures system maintainability and compliance.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 7
2 Quality metrics
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-022
TITLE: Quality Metrics
STATEMENT: The development shall track quality metrics including defect density, code coverage, safety metrics, and performance metrics for continuous quality improvement.
RATIONALE: Quality metrics ensure continuous quality improvement and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 8
 Risk management
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-023
TITLE: Risk Management Process
STATEMENT: The development shall include comprehensive risk management processes with risk identification, risk assessment, risk mitigation, and risk monitoring throughout the development lifecycle.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive risk management ensures successful project execution and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 9
 Notes
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDP-024
TITLE: Development Guidelines
STATEMENT: The development shall follow automotive safety development guidelines, industry best practices, and continuous improvement processes for quality assurance and safety compliance.
RATIONALE: Development guidelines provide guidance for development teams and ensure quality and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
